     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas this a transcription error? These are some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is a more typical starting or maintenance dose\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, and I'll enter it. If you do confirm it, I'll add a note to the order saying the dose was verified."
      }
     ],
